  "title": "Routes in the knot's spaces are fixed by the space and carry one bit at most",
  "subject": "Whether paths through the hubs of a knot's space are fixed by the law or chosen by an observer, and what they carry",
  "conclusion": "Every nontrivial 3-edge cut of a knot's space is a proper splice cut or a shifted 2-edge cut, and in ten spaces proper cuts never cross, so the parts and routes are fixed by the space. A route through atoms carries its length mod 2 and a route through a hub nothing beyond it; cutting both routes separates, and these are routes of a declared substrate, not native paths of contacts.",
